he closing of the Business Combination, our ordinary shares and public warrants began trading on the Nasdaq Capital Market LLC (“Nasdaq”) under the ticker symbols “ZOOZ” and “ZOOZW”, respectively, on April 5, 2024.","context":"Company Overview","section":"AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":8,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-040046","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-25","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001992818","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1992818/000149315226040046/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/2735e4421e3b7b825a4e4ce4857f5bab309c68bcde4fc25133510ffb60354fd0.bin","sha256":"2735e4421e3b7b825a4e4ce4857f5bab309c68bcde4fc25133510ffb60354fd0"}},{"id":"49ba49428dee5d3e261d24b69ee2282f4f58345938e9e4a9baf2a06c95092576","quote":"On July 29, 2025, the Company entered into securities purchase agreements with certain institutional and accredited investors for the Private Placement consisting of ordinary shares, pre-funded warrants, and warrants. Following the entry into the Private Placement, the Company adopted bitcoin as its primary treasury reserve asset, subject to market conditions and its anticipated cash needs. Under this strategy, the Company may acquire and hold bitcoin using cash flows in excess of working capital requirements and subject to market conditions, raise capital through equity or debt offerings with proceeds used to purchase bitcoin.","context":"On April 4, 2024, Keyarch Acquisition Corporation and the Company consummated their previously announced Business Combination pursuant to that certain Business Combination Agreement (the “Business Combination”), pursuant to which Keyarch became a direct, wholly-owned subsidiary of ZOOZ. In connection with the closing of the Business Combination, our ordinary shares and public warrants began trading on the Nasdaq Capital Market LLC (“Nasdaq”) under the ticker symbols “ZOOZ” and “ZOOZW”, respectively, on April 5, 2024.","section":"AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":9,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-040046","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-25","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001992818","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1992818/000149315226040046/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/2735e4421e3b7b825a4e4ce4857f5bab309c68bcde4fc25133510ffb60354fd0.bin","sha256":"2735e4421e3b7b825a4e4ce4857f5bab309c68bcde4fc25133510ffb60354fd0"}},{"id":"e2cbfa903c4e924a96c13e11e02d7057aeba8eb45283e2c740d83ebfdb259205","quote":"The Company currently operates primarily as a bitcoin treasury company, and to a lesser extent, continues to operate in developing, producing, marketing, and selling systems that manage and optimize power delivery to clusters of ultra-fast EV chargers (the “Legacy Business”) and seeks to commercialize its EV ultra-fast charging infrastructure and related technology, and it is exploring strategic alternatives to capitalize on its patented flywheel technology.","context":"On July 29, 2025, the Company entered into securities purchase agreements with certain institutional and accredited investors for the Private Placement consisting of ordinary shares, pre-funded warrants, and warrants. Following the entry into the Private Placement, the Company adopted bitcoin as its primary treasury reserve asset, subject to market conditions and its anticipated cash needs. Under this strategy, the Company may acquire and hold bitcoin using cash flows in excess of working capital requirements and subject to market conditions, raise capital through equity or debt offerings with proceeds used to purchase bitcoin.","section":"AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":10,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-040046","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-25","reportDate":"2026-0